A||N||5||count_iblis||Remembering the fiero||||1||
Z||000000||count_iblis||10-06-2000||09:00 AM||||I was just wondering what everyone's <P>thoughts were when they saw the fiero for <P>the first time.  <P>I was about 14 yrs old when my love for cars <P>started to sink in,  I was always in love <P>with the Mustang.  But one day my mom and dad<P>were going out that day to buy my sister a <P>new car, I asked her what she was going to <P>get and she said she was leaning toward a <P>Fiero.  I was like oh my gawd your getting a <P>a ferarri?  She was like nope something <P>something sorta like on but it is called <P>Fiero.  At that time i had always seen a <P>Fiero but didnt know what they were called<P>I always thought they were some extoic car <P>that came out.  So when she came home in <P>new  87 coupe i fell in love with it!  It <P>was a red auto with a sunroof.  I begged her<P>to take me out in it every where she went. <P>But she always said she was going to pic up <P>a friend of hers and there was only two <P>seats!  So I washed the car ever chance i got<P>and sometimes just sat in the drivers seat <P>acting like a was driving it around.  Since <P>then i have owned several cars (18 to be <P>count)  but still the fiero is a the top of <P>my list as the best and most fun cars to <P>drive.<P><BR>Sorry for the long post just thought it would<P>be nice to share this with other Fiero <P>lovers!<P><BR>COUNT<P>countiblis@yahoo.com<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||10-06-2000||10:05 AM||||I was only 10 when the Fiero came out, I remember my father talking about how he wanted one. He never did buy one though. <BR>I don't remember exactly when I fell in love with them. <BR>I bought my first one at 16, it was an 84 base model with a/c and sunroof. I worshipped that car. I bought turbo wheels for it and a spoiler. I detailed it three times a week. Then I bought an 84SE then an 86GT. Then I heard about the 88's redesigned suspension and I just had to have one, so I called Bob at Kickhill and he had an 88GT T-top that was hit in the passenger side, I went up the next day, my mother thought I was crazy to drive 8 hours to go see a wrecked car. Well, I bought that car and Bob gave me everything I needed to make it whole again. <P>Well I hope my long post didn't put anyone to sleep. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||count_iblis||10-06-2000||10:31 PM||||comon ladies and gents, dont be shy tell ol count what you first thoughts and feelings were with the fiero||||reg||1
Z||000003||overlord||10-06-2000||11:03 PM||||well ok...<P>i first saw my fiero way back when i was 19.<BR>A whole 3 years ago!<P>that was the first time i ever saw one, had noo idead what it was....that it was some foreign thing.<BR>But the price was right and i needed a car bad so i just upped and  bought it..<P>MAN AM I GLAD I DID!<BR>i know so much about these little cars now<BR>kinda wish everyone did.||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-06-2000||11:58 PM||||The first time I can really remember seeing one (taking notice that is) was around 86..I was 14 and was watching Ferris Buellers Day Off...Jennifer Grey drove a white one. I thought it was kinda cool, however at the time I was seriously into (of all things) Jaguars! My best friends mom had one, and I thought it was the most beautiful car I had ever seen (and to an extent, still do).<BR>Anyway, a couple of years later, a friend of mine bought one. This was in mid 1988..it was an 84...red w/ grey int., auto, sunroof, luggage rack. I ended up buying that thing from him. I remember liking it, but at the time I was 16 and my friends were wanting me to take them everywhere..because I had a license, not because I had a Fiero, they couldve cared less. Unfortunantly, it only had two seats (duh), and I wanted to tote several friends around at a time, plus it was hard as he11 to, well, you know, with the girls!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So I ended up selling it, and my dad gave me his 78 Trans Am. Man, that thing was sweet!!! (To this day I still regret getting rid of it, I traded it in 95 for a brand new Camaro, which I only had for 6 months!)<BR>Anyway alittle over a year ago a friend of mine (my roommate now, with the mustang) was talking about how he was looking for a second car to keep the miles off his Mustang. We were talking and he said "hey remember Tracy's (his old g/f) Fiero she used to have?" Thats all it took, he bought one, and the rest is history! Now weve got zillions of them! lol    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-06-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-07-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000005||Cheever2||10-07-2000||08:55 PM||||First I saw one was walking thru a store parking lot.  Walked right next to it, first noticed how low it was, then the fact that it was a 2-seater, then saw the interior.  Was really impressed with the wide center arm rest/console and wondered what it would feel like to sit in it.  Some mechanic I knew said you couldn't get parts for them, so he killed my interest.  Was years before I finally tried one on for size.  The rest is a continual love affair saga/epic/whatever.<BR>   ||||reg||1
